WEBVTT

00:03:28.345 --> 00:03:31.479
Why does any of this matter at all?

00:03:31.479 --> 00:03:33.950
Well first of all, it's already allowing us

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.151
to shift towards preventive,

00:03:36.151 --> 00:03:38.029
condition-based maintenance,

00:03:38.029 --> 00:03:39.991
which means fixing machines

00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:42.279
just before they break,

00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:44.295
without wasting time

00:03:44.295 --> 00:03:46.623
servicing them on a fixed schedule.

00:03:46.623 --> 00:03:50.260
And this, in turn, is pushing us towards

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.115
zero unplanned downtime,

00:03:52.115 --> 00:03:54.980
which means there will be no more power outages,

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.020
no more flight delays.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.664
So let me give you a few examples

00:03:58.664 --> 00:04:00.543
of how these brilliant machines work,